--TEST--
Both members that are asked *about* a job take the receipt itself, so neither of them can be handed a bare row number — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The agreement first: one receipt, two members, and each takes it whole. That
// is what `Core\Queue\Id` is the name for — a job is a row *and* a queue, and
// a member taking only the row would have to take the queue beside it or
// search every queue for it.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");

bool $won = Core\Queue::cancel($receipt);
Core\Queue\State $state = Core\Queue::status($receipt);

// So the number `push` actually wrote is not something a program is ever
// holding, and this line is what says so.
bool $late = Core\Queue::cancel(7);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Queue\Id`, found `int`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
